## Gmail Integration Doctrine (Multi‑Tenant, No Manual Setup)

- Provider Abstraction
  - Define `EmailProvider` interface: `auth()`, `fetchHistory()`, `backfill()`, `listThreads()`, `listMessages()`, `send()`.
  - Implement `GmailProvider` first; keep interface generic for Outlook later.

- OAuth & Tokens
  - User-level OAuth 2.0 with offline access (refresh tokens); minimal scopes (read, send).
  - Optional Workspace mode: domain-wide delegation via service account for enterprise tenants.
  - Store tokens per site/user encrypted; auto-refresh; revoke on disconnect.

- Sync Strategy
  - Default: incremental polling (Gmail `history.list` + `messages.get`) on short cadence with jitter/backoff.
  - Advanced: Gmail Pub/Sub push; Terraform module to provision topic/subscription + webhook endpoint.
  - Idempotency by `provider_message_id`, `provider_thread_id`.

- Data Model (DocTypes)
  - `Communication Provider Account` (provider, user, tokens, scopes, status).
  - `Mailbox Connection` (label, backfill window, state, rate limits).
  - `Provider Sync Cursor` (historyId, last_synced_at, backoff state).

- Ingestion & Send Paths
  - Backfill N days; then incremental sync using historyId.
  - Send via Gmail API; persist `provider_message_id` and `provider_thread_id` for linking.

- Onboarding UX
  - "Connect Gmail" → OAuth → choose backfill window → test send.
  - No per-user manual API setup; admin-only path for Workspace service account if enabled.

- Security & Multi‑Tenancy
  - Site-scoped credentials; least-privileged scopes per role.
  - Role gates for connect, backfill, send; audit trails for connect/sync/send actions.

- Observability
  - Metrics: sync latency, items/min, error rate; alerts for stuck cursors or token failures.
  - Logs for token refresh, retries, webhook delivery; dashboards per tenant.

- Deployment (Frappe Cloud)
  - App config for OAuth client ID/secret (Integrations settings or env).
  - Optional Terraform for Pub/Sub setup; polling remains the default fallback.

- Rollout Plan
  - M1: Polling-only Gmail (OAuth, backfill+incremental, send).
  - M2: Pub/Sub + Terraform; webhook handler + validation.
  - M3: Workspace admin mode; per-tenant rate limits & dashboards.
  - M4: Outlook provider under same interface.